        }
      }
    },
    "the_finding": "on BTC the two rungs are the same number on almost every row, because the whole visible book ends inside the inner one; on ETH they differ by about a third. A ladder of two rungs is therefore a ladder of one rung on one of the two coins, and its shape would be a property of where the rungs were put rather than of the book",
    "what_was_read_instead": "every snapshot of every cached hour, twenty levels a side, giving the shape at a quarter of a basis point, which is finer than one tick on either coin",
    "measured_cost": "about two and a half minutes, printed by every run"
  },
